  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "In a medium bowl, combine dried white corn, butter, onion, garlic, paprika, salt, and black pepper, and toss to coat.",
    "Place a large piece of parchment paper on a baking sheet, and arrange the corn mixture in the center.",
    "Fold the parchment paper over the corn mixture, and crimp the edges to seal the papillote.",
    "Bake for 20 minutes, or until the corn is tender and fragrant.",
    "Remove the papillote from the oven, and sprinkle with parsley, dill, and lemon juice.",
    "Let the papillote rest for 2 minutes, then slice it in half, and serve.",
    "Garnish with additional parsley and dill, if desired.",
    "Serve the papillote hot, with a side of your choice, such as rice, salad, or grilled meat."
